/**
 *  @page WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_EXPLORER WeAct STM32G030 CLI Explorer
 *
 *  A command-line processor laboratory for the WeAct STM32G030F6P6/F8P6 core
 *  board. It follows the style of the ST Nucleo and px_hero `cli_explorer`
 *  applications while using only peripherals present on this board.
 *
 *  Build the 32 KB STM32G030x6 image:
 *
 *      make build=debug
 *
 *  Build the 64 KB STM32G030x8 image:
 *
 *      make clean
 *      make build=debug FLASH_SIZE=64k
 *
 *  The terminal is USART1 at 115200 8N1 on PA11 TX and PA12 RX.
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_ROOT Root commands
 *
 *      help [prefix]          List commands or matching help
 *      info                   Report device ID, clocks and board pin map
 *      led on|off|toggle      Control the active-low onboard LED on PA4
 *      beep <ms> [Hz]         Generate a tone on PA3
 *      delay <n> [ms|s]       Exercise the calibrated blocking delay
 *      rst                    Reset the microcontroller
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_ADC ADC
 *
 *      adc info               Report ADC configuration and channel map
 *      adc s <ch> [interval]  Sample once or continuously
 *      adc bin <ch>           Print a 12-bit binary sample
 *      adc all                Sample PA0 through PA3
 *      adc v <mV>             Set the voltage scaling reference assumption
 *
 *  External ADC channels are 0/PA0, 1/PA1, 2/PA2, and 3/PA3. The driver also
 *  accepts `ch16`, `ch17`, and `ch18` for the MCU's internal channels when
 *  supported by the selected silicon. A continuous sample stops on the PA14
 *  button or on the next received byte.
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_GPIO GPIO
 *
 *      gpio info <pin|all|regs>
 *      gpio ci <pin> [pu|pd]
 *      gpio co <pin> <0|1> [od] [pu]
 *      gpio af <pin> <0..7>
 *      gpio ana <pin>
 *      gpio i <pin>
 *      gpio o <pin> <0|1>
 *
 *  Pins use names such as `a0`, `b0`, `c14`, or these aliases: `led`, `button`,
 *  `adc0`..`adc3`, `spi_cs`, `spi_sck`, `spi_miso`, and `spi_mosi`.
 *  `gpio info regs` reports the GPIOA/B/C register state.
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_UART UART
 *
 *      uart info
 *      uart cfg 1 <baud> [7|8|9] [n|o|e] [1|2]
 *      uart w <d0> .. [d15]
 *      uart r <count> <timeout ms>
 *      uart x <count> <timeout ms> <d0> .. [d15]
 *      uart s <timeout ms> <string> [cr|lf|crlf]
 *      uart err
 *
 *  UART test commands use the same USART1 as the CLI. Add an external TX-to-RX
 *  loopback wire if testing receive or exchange commands. Reconfiguring the
 *  port also reconfigures the command terminal.
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_SPI SPI
 *
 *      spi cfg [1] [cs] [baud] [mode] [lsb|msb]
 *      spi cs lo|hi
 *      spi w <d0> .. [d7]
 *      spi r <count>
 *      spi x <d0> .. [d7]
 *
 *  SPI1 uses PA5 SCK, PA6 MISO, PA7 MOSI, and PA8 as the default manual CS.
 *  The application supports one SPI peripheral and a user-selectable GPIO CS.
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_RTC RTC
 *
 *      rtc r
 *      rtc w <yy-mm-dd> <hh:mm:ss>
 *
 *  The board LSE on PC14/PC15 is used as the RTC clock source.
 *
 *  @section WEACT_STM32G030_CLI_MEM Memory
 *
 *      mem r <b|w|l> <address> [count]
 *      mem w <b|w|l> <address> <d0> .. [d7]
 *      mem d <address> <number of bytes>
 *
 *  These commands intentionally expose the memory-mapped processor address
 *  space for hardware investigation. Invalid addresses or writes to protected
 *  registers can fault or change the board state; use the reference manual.
 */
